---
title: Rigatoni with lamb sugo
tags: [italian, lamb, make-ahead, weekend]
cuisine: italian
source: Rigatoni all'Agnello by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/rigatoni-allagnello
---

> A restaurant recipe: the sugo and anchovy butter are large batches, and the
> amounts under "Each plate" are for one serving.

== Lamb sugo ==

Tie the @Parmigiano Reggiano rinds{100%g}, @rosemary leaves{10%g} and
@thyme{3%g} in a sachet.

Pass the @yellow onions{200%g}(peeled, finely chopped),
@carrots{100%g}(peeled, diced), @celery{100%g}(diced) and
@garlic{30%g}(minced) through a #meat grinder{} with a coarse die.

Brown the @ground lamb{1.45%kg} in batches in a #rondeau{} over medium-high
heat and set it aside in a #hotel pan{}.

Cook the ground vegetables in the rondeau with a little @kosher salt{} until
lightly caramelized. Add the @whole peeled tomatoes{540%g} and
@tomato paste{33%g}, then deglaze with the @red wine{2%l}.

Bring to a boil, return the lamb, add the sachet, and simmer ~{2%hours},
stirring now and then.

Season with @MSG{10%g}, @Worcestershire sauce{5%g}, @colatura{5%g} and
@balsamic vinegar{40%ml}(essenza). Cool and refrigerate.

== Anchovy butter ==

Blend the @unsalted butter{2%lb}(cubed), @anchovy fillets{90%g} and
@lemon zest{12%g} in a #food processor{} until smooth. Refrigerate.

== Each plate ==

Warm a portion of the sugo in a #small saucepan{} over low heat.

Toss the @broccoli rabe{45%g} with @extra virgin olive oil{}, @kosher salt{}
and @black pepper{}, and grill until charred and tender. Cool, then chop into
1/2 cm pieces.

Boil the @rigatoni{100%g} in salted water until just al dente. Drain, keeping
some of the water.

In a #sauté pan{} over medium heat, combine the pasta, the warm sugo, the
broccoli rabe, @pecorino cheese{13%g}(Sardo, grated), @lemon juice{15%g},
@cherry peppers{5%g}(chopped) and a spoon of anchovy butter. Loosen with pasta
water and cook until the sauce clings. Adjust with salt and lemon juice.

Serve in a shallow bowl with more grated pecorino, the
@lemon olive oil{6%g}, @basil leaves{3%g} and @mint leaves{2%g}.
